{
  "facts": [
    {
      "topic": "target_route",
      "statement": "The harness treats the first eight bytes as options and width, then passes the remaining bytes as Markdown through document, file, incremental parser, or markdown-to-HTML mode.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 60, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "configuration",
      "statement": "The harness masks options to the listed bits, including CMARK_OPT_VALIDATE_UTF8; a zero options field leaves UTF-8 validation disabled.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 30, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "trigger",
      "statement": "With UTF-8 validation disabled, line processing copies input bytes into the current line. The feed routine has special handling for line endings and NUL, but its shown handling does not transform a raw 0xFF byte.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-f20dc521c971d4f66630", "start_line": 1279, "end_line": 1299, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-e84b4d565106bb8a042f", "start_line": 596, "end_line": 648, "role": "dependency", "dependency_reason": "Shows how supplied bytes are split into lines and how NUL is replaced before line processing."}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "contract",
      "statement": "In the after scanner, high bytes including 0xFF are included in the quoted-attribute scan loops. A closing quote, `>`, and line ending can lead to the scanner returning HTML block type 7.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-a1a08cffd1ca26310e68", "start_line": 7167, "end_line": 7176, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-a1a08cffd1ca26310e68", "start_line": 7434, "end_line": 7483, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-a1a08cffd1ca26310e68", "start_line": 7314, "end_line": 7385, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "counterevidence",
      "statement": "In the before scanner, a raw 0xFF inside the quoted-value state is outside the accepted high-byte range and takes the rejection path rather than completing that HTML block type 7 match.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-b355481778f3add37dfc", "start_line": 8017, "end_line": 8026, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-b355481778f3add37dfc", "start_line": 8356, "end_line": 8388, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-b355481778f3add37dfc", "start_line": 8057, "end_line": 8063, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-b355481778f3add37dfc", "start_line": 8028, "end_line": 8032, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "scope",
      "statement": "Line processing calls open_new_blocks after checking open blocks. The supplied line-processing code does not show the guards or use of the type 7 scanner result inside open_new_blocks.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-f20dc521c971d4f66630", "start_line": 1299, "end_line": 1313, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "alternative",
      "statement": "The harness has several parsing routes for the same Markdown bytes, including direct document parsing, file parsing, incremental feeding, and markdown-to-HTML conversion. Whether any route reaches the specified HTML block behavior depends on the missing caller control flow.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 62, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "consequence",
      "statement": "If an HTML block node is created, HTML rendering distinguishes it from a paragraph: without CMARK_OPT_UNSAFE it emits a raw-HTML-omitted marker, and with that option it emits the node bytes.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-996d9a66e32c87a8332b", "start_line": 175, "end_line": 183, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-996d9a66e32c87a8332b", "start_line": 203, "end_line": 221, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c", "start_line": 64, "end_line": 71, "role": "dependency", "dependency_reason": "The harness renders HTML for a non-null parsed document."}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "configuration",
      "statement": "The supplied recipe invokes CMake with no added options, builds cmark_static, compiles the harness, and links it with libcmark.a.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-944c463f7c78bc0977c2", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 25, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "counterevidence",
      "statement": "The complete harness contains no assertion that checks whether this input was classified as an HTML block. Its document-dependent rendering is gated by `doc != NULL`.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 75, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""}
      ],
      "absence_claim": true,
      "audited_unit_ids": ["u-01d44c1169261cd79a4c"]
    }
  ],
  "missing_information": [
    "The before and after `open_new_blocks` control flow in `src/blocks.c`, including guards on `scan_html_block_start_7` and how its result creates an HTML block."
  ],
  "requested_symbols": ["open_new_blocks"],
  "requested_paths": ["src/blocks.c"]
}
